A goroutine clears the captured err when it is ErrDeclined, and the function waits for it.
Precise answer: ErrInternal only. Guards across a goroutine boundary cannot be trusted and the captured
variable escapes (out of documented scope): the tool reports one unresolved(memory) entry and no origins.
